    "title": "Saul “enquired of the LORD”, and Saul “enquired not of the LORD”",
    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "1 Samuel 28:6 says Saul enquired of the LORD and got no answer. 1 Chronicles 10:14 gives as a reason for his death that he “enquired not of the LORD”.",
    "text": "KJV 1 Samuel 28:6: “And when Saul enquired of the Lord, the Lord answered him not”. KJV 1 Chronicles 10:14: “And enquired not of the Lord: therefore he slew him”. Hebrew (WLC) 1 Samuel 28:6: וַיִּשְׁאַ֤ל שָׁאוּל֙ בַּֽיהוָ֔ה [and Saul asked of the LORD]; 1 Chronicles 10:14: וְלֹֽא־דָרַ֥שׁ בַּֽיהוָ֖ה [and he did not seek the LORD]; 1 Chronicles 10:13 ends לִשְׁאֹ֥ול בָּאֹ֖וב לִדְרֹֽושׁ [to ask of a medium, to seek]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/9/28/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/13/10/.",
    "reasoning": "In the KJV the same English verb is affirmed in Samuel and denied in Chronicles.",
    "scope": "The Hebrew uses two different verbs, “asked” in Samuel and “sought” in Chronicles, so the Hebrew does not affirm and deny the same word; 1 Chronicles 10:13 uses both verbs together for consulting the medium. Chronicles may mean that Saul did not seek the LORD in earnest or did not keep seeking. The contrast is clear in the KJV wording and weaker in the Hebrew. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text; a digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees.",
