    "summary": "1 Samuel 15 says Saul struck the Amalekites as far as Shur and utterly destroyed all the people. Later David raids Amalekites on the way to Shur, and Amalekites burn Ziklag.",
    "text": "KJV 1 Samuel 15:7: “And Saul smote the Amalekites from Havilah until thou comest to Shur, that is over against Egypt.” KJV 15:8: “and utterly destroyed all the people with the edge of the sword”. KJV 27:8: “invaded the Geshurites, and the Gezrites, and the Amalekites: for those nations were of old the inhabitants of the land, as thou goest to Shur, even unto the land of Egypt”. KJV 30:1: “the Amalekites had invaded the south, and Ziklag, and smitten Ziklag, and burned it with fire”. Hebrew (WLC) 15:8: וְאֶת־כָּל־הָעָ֖ם הֶחֱרִ֥ים לְפִי־חָֽרֶב [and all the people he devoted to destruction by the edge of the sword]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/9/15/.",
