    "summary": "1 Kings counts 550 chief officers ruling over the workers. 2 Chronicles counts 250.",
    "text": "KJV 1 Kings 9:23: “five hundred and fifty, which bare rule over the people that wrought in the work”. Hebrew (WLC): חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים וַחֲמֵ֣שׁ מֵאֹ֑ות [fifty and five hundred]. KJV 2 Chronicles 8:10: “And these were the chief of king Solomon's officers, even two hundred and fifty, that bare rule over the people.” Hebrew (WLC) 2 Chronicles 8:10: חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים וּמָאתָ֑יִם [fifty and two hundred]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 2 Chronicles 8:10: πεντήκοντα καὶ διακόσιοι [fifty and two hundred]. The Brenton Greek page for 1 Kings 9 prints verses 1–9, 9a, 10–14 and 26–28; it has no verse 23. Fetched from https://ebible.org/grcbrent/1KI09.htm, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/11/9/, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/14/8/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/2CH08.htm.",
