    "summary": "1 Kings says that under Jehoshaphat “the high places were not taken away”. 2 Chronicles 17 says he took them away out of Judah. 2 Chronicles 20 says they were not taken away.",
    "text": "KJV 1 Kings 22:43: “nevertheless the high places were not taken away; for the people offered and burnt incense yet in the high places”. Hebrew (WLC), where this half-verse is numbered 22:44: אַ֥ךְ הַבָּמֹ֖ות לֹֽא־סָ֑רוּ [only the high places were not removed]. KJV 2 Chronicles 17:6: “moreover he took away the high places and groves out of Judah”. Hebrew (WLC) 2 Chronicles 17:6: וְעֹ֗וד הֵסִ֛יר אֶת־הַבָּמֹ֥ות וְאֶת־הָאֲשֵׁרִ֖ים מִיהוּדָֽה [and further he removed the high places and the Asherim from Judah]. KJV 2 Chronicles 20:33: “Howbeit the high places were not taken away”. Hebrew (WLC) 2 Chronicles 20:33: אַ֥ךְ הַבָּמֹ֖ות לֹא־סָ֑רוּ. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/11/22/, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/14/17/ and https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/14/20/.",
