    "id": "baasha-dead-by-asa-twenty-sixth-year-or-attacking-in-thirty-sixth",
    "mode": "contradictions",
    "ref": "1 Kings 16:8",
    "appliesTo": [
      "1 Kings 16:8",
      "2 Chronicles 16:1"
    ],
    "title": "Baasha: dead by Asa’s twenty-sixth year, or attacking Judah in his thirty-sixth?",
    "status": "Textual conflict",
    "summary": "In 1 Kings Baasha dies and his son succeeds him in the twenty-sixth year of Asa. In 2 Chronicles Baasha marches against Judah in Asa’s thirty-sixth year. The Greek of Chronicles has the thirty-eighth year.",
    "text": "KJV 1 Kings 15:33: “In the third year of Asa king of Judah began Baasha the son of Ahijah to reign over all Israel in Tirzah, twenty and four years.” KJV 16:6: “So Baasha slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirzah: and Elah his son reigned in his stead.” KJV 16:8: “In the twenty and sixth year of Asa king of Judah began Elah the son of Baasha to reign over Israel”. Hebrew (WLC) 16:8: בִּשְׁנַ֨ת עֶשְׂרִ֤ים וָשֵׁשׁ֙ שָׁנָ֔ה לְאָסָ֖א מֶ֣לֶךְ יְהוּדָ֑ה [in the twenty-sixth year of Asa king of Judah]. KJV 2 Chronicles 16:1: “In the six and thirtieth year of the reign of Asa Baasha king of Israel came up against Judah, and built Ramah”. Hebrew (WLC) 2 Chronicles 16:1: בִּשְׁנַ֨ת שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים וָשֵׁשׁ֙ לְמַלְכ֣וּת אָסָ֔א עָלָ֞ה בַּעְשָׁ֤א מֶֽלֶךְ־יִשְׂרָאֵל֙ עַל־יְהוּדָ֔ה [in the thirty-sixth year of the reign of Asa, Baasha king of Israel came up against Judah]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 2 Chronicles 16:1: Καὶ ἐν τῷ ὀγδόῳ καὶ τριακοστῷ ἔτει τῆς βασιλείας Ἀσὰ, ἀνέβη βασιλεὺς Ἰσραὴλ ἐπὶ Ἰούδαν [and in the thirty-eighth year of the reign of Asa, the king of Israel came up against Judah]; 16:3 names him: τὸν Βαασὰ βασιλέα Ἰσραὴλ. Brenton Greek 1 Kings 16:8: Καὶ Ἠλὰ υἱὸς Βαασὰ ἐβασίλευσεν ἐπὶ Ἰσραὴλ δύο ἔτη ἐν Θερσᾷ. [and Ela son of Baasa reigned over Israel two years in Thersa]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/11/16/, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/14/16/, https://ebible.org/grcbrent/2CH16.htm and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/1KI16.htm.",
    "reasoning": "Kings starts Baasha in Asa’s third year, gives him twenty-four years, and dates his son’s accession to Asa’s twenty-sixth. Chronicles has Baasha build Ramah ten years after that. Brenton’s Greek of 2 Chronicles 16:1 has a different year from the KJV, and it is later still; Brenton’s Greek of 1 Kings 16:8 has no year of Asa at all.",
    "scope": "G applies at 2 Chronicles 16:1 for the year, and at 1 Kings 16:8 for the missing date. Counting the thirty-six years from a point earlier than Asa’s accession would remove the clash; the verse says “of the reign of Asa”. The Greek of 16:1 does not name the king of Israel in that verse and names Baasha two verses later. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
