    "text": "KJV 1 Kings 20:38: “and disguised himself with ashes upon his face”. KJV 20:41: “And he hasted, and took the ashes away from his face”. Septuagint (Brenton Greek), which numbers this chapter 21, verse 21:38: καὶ κατεδήσατο ἐν τελαμῶνι τοὺς ὀφθαλμοὺς αὐτοῦ; 21:41: καὶ ἀφεῖλε τὸν τελαμῶνα ἀπὸ τῶν ὀφθαλμῶν αὐτοῦ. Brenton’s English translation of the same, 21:38: “and bound his eyes with a bandage”; 21:41: “and took away the bandage from his eyes”. Hebrew (WLC) 20:38: וַיִּתְחַפֵּ֥שׂ בָּאֲפֵ֖ר עַל־עֵינָֽיו. Fetched from https://ebible.org/grcbrent/1KI21.htm, https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/1KI21.htm and https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/11/20/.",
