    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "Jeremiah says the Lord declared that Jehoiakim would have none to sit on David’s throne. 2 Kings says his son Jehoiachin reigned in his stead, for three months.",
    "text": "KJV Jeremiah 36:30: “Therefore thus saith the Lord of Jehoiakim king of Judah; He shall have none to sit upon the throne of David”. Hebrew (WLC) Jeremiah 36:30: לֹא־יִֽהְיֶה־לֹּ֥ו יֹושֵׁ֖ב עַל־כִּסֵּ֣א דָוִ֑ד [he shall not have one sitting on the throne of David]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek), numbered Jeremiah 43:30: οὐκ ἔσται αὐτῷ καθήμενος ἐπὶ θρόνου Δαυὶδ [he shall not have one sitting on the throne of David]. KJV 2 Kings 24:6: “So Jehoiakim slept with his fathers: and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his stead.” Hebrew (WLC) 24:6: וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ יְהֹויָכִ֥ין בְּנֹ֖ו תַּחְתָּֽיו [and Jehoiachin his son reigned in his place]. Brenton Greek 24:6: καὶ ἐβασίλευσεν Ἰωακεὶμ υἱὸς αὐτοῦ ἀντʼ αὐτοῦ [and Joakim his son reigned in his place]. KJV 24:8: “Jehoiachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, and he reigned in Jerusalem three months.” Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/24/36/, https://ebible.org/grcbrent/JER43.htm, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/12/24/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/2KI24.htm.",
