    "scope": "No tag is proposed: the KJV matches the Hebrew in both books, and the Greek agrees. Both statements can stand if a reign of three months, ended by exile, is not counted as sitting on the throne, or if the prophecy looks to a lasting line; neither book says so. Brenton’s Greek numbers this chapter of Jeremiah 43. The second half of Jeremiah 36:30, about Jehoiakim’s body, is not compared here. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
