    "scope": "No tag is proposed: the KJV matches the Hebrew in each book, and Brenton’s Greek has the seventh in Kings and the tenth in Jeremiah. The Greek of Jeremiah 52:12 has no “nineteenth year”; that is not the subject of this record. Both days can stand if one marks arrival near the city and the other entry into it; both verses use the same verb and neither says so. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
