    "id": "benjamin-ten-sons-or-sons-and-grandsons-greek",
    "mode": "contradictions",
    "ref": "Genesis 46:21",
    "appliesTo": [
      "Genesis 46:21"
    ],
    "title": "Naaman and Ard: sons of Benjamin, or sons of Bela?",
    "status": "Textual conflict",
    "summary": "Genesis in the KJV lists ten sons of Benjamin, among them Naaman and Ard. Numbers calls Ard and Naaman sons of Bela, Benjamin’s son. Brenton’s Greek of Genesis gives Benjamin three sons and makes the rest sons of Bala and one a son of Gera.",
    "text": "KJV Genesis 46:21: “And the sons of Benjamin were Belah, and Becher, and Ashbel, Gera, and Naaman, Ehi, and Rosh, Muppim, and Huppim, and Ard.” Hebrew (WLC) 46:21: וּבְנֵ֣י בִנְיָמִ֗ן בֶּ֤לַע וָבֶ֙כֶר֙ וְאַשְׁבֵּ֔ל גֵּרָ֥א וְנַעֲמָ֖ן אֵחִ֣י וָרֹ֑אשׁ מֻפִּ֥ים וְחֻפִּ֖ים וָאָֽרְדְּ [and the sons of Benjamin: Bela and Becher and Ashbel, Gera and Naaman, Ehi and Rosh, Muppim and Huppim and Ard]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 46:21: Υἱοὶ δὲ Βενιαμεὶν, Βαλὰ καὶ Βοχὸρ, καὶ Ἀσβήλ. Ἐγένοντο δὲ υἱοὶ Βαλὰ, Γηρὰ, καὶ Νοεμὰν, καὶ Ἀγχὶς, καὶ Ῥὼς, καὶ Μαμφίμ· Γηρὰ δὲ ἐγέννησε τὸν Ἀράδ. [and the sons of Benjamin: Bala and Bochor and Asbel. And the sons of Bala were Gera and Noeman and Anchis and Ros and Mamphim; and Gera begat Arad]. KJV Numbers 26:38, as packaged: “The sons of Benjamin after their families: of Bela, the family of the Belaites”. KJV Numbers 26:40, as packaged: “And the sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman”. Hebrew (WLC) Numbers 26:40: וַיִּהְי֥וּ בְנֵי־בֶ֖לַע אַ֣רְדְּ וְנַעֲמָ֑ן [and the sons of Bela were Ard and Naaman]. Brenton Greek, printed as Numbers 26:44: Καὶ ἐγένοντο οἱ υἱοὶ Βαλὲ, Ἀδὰρ, καὶ Νοεμάν [and the sons of Bale were Adar and Noeman]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/1/46/, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/4/26/, https://ebible.org/grcbrent/GEN46.htm and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/NUM26.htm.",
    "reasoning": "In the KJV of Genesis, Naaman and Ard stand in a list headed “the sons of Benjamin”. In the KJV of Numbers they are sons of Bela, and so Benjamin’s grandsons. The KJV follows the Hebrew in both books. Brenton’s Greek of Genesis divides the list: three sons of Benjamin, five sons of Bala including Noeman, and Arad as a son of Gera. It names nine men where the KJV names ten, and it agrees with Numbers that Noeman is Bala’s son.",
    "scope": "G applies at Genesis 46:21, where the Greek differs from the KJV. The two KJV verses can be reconciled if “sons” in Genesis takes in grandsons, or if there were two men of each name; Genesis says neither. Whether Arad in the Greek of Genesis and Adar in the Greek of Numbers are the same name is not settled here. The total of persons in Genesis 46 is not examined in this record. The supplied KJV source prints “Ard” at Numbers 26:40; the packaged verse and this quotation were corrected together to match it. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
