    "scope": "G applies at Exodus 1:11. This is a difference between two published texts; the KJV does not say that only two cities were built, so the two statements can both stand. No claim is made about which list is original or about the history of any of the three cities. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
