    "scope": "G applies at Exodus 15:3. The verse is a line of a song, and this record compares its wording in two published texts; it draws no conclusion from the image itself. The two wordings can both be held: one who ends wars may do so by fighting. No claim is made about which wording is original. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
