    "title": "“Ye shall not eat any thing with the blood” — the Greek says “on the mountains”",
    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV, with the Hebrew, forbids eating “with the blood”. Brenton’s Greek of the same verse has no blood: it forbids eating “on the mountains”.",
    "text": "KJV Leviticus 19:26: “Ye shall not eat any thing with the blood: neither shall ye use enchantment, nor observe times.” Hebrew (WLC) 19:26: לֹ֥א תֹאכְל֖וּ עַל־הַדָּ֑ם [you shall not eat upon the blood]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 19:26: Μὴ ἔσθετε ἐπὶ τῶν ὀρέων [do not eat upon the mountains]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/3/19/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/LEV19.htm.",
