    "title": "The congregation sins in ignorance: a bullock as the sin offering, or a bullock burnt and a kid as the sin offering?",
    "status": "Textual conflict",
    "summary": "Leviticus says that when the whole congregation sins through ignorance it offers a young bullock, and calls it “a sin offering for the congregation”. Numbers says that for a thing done in ignorance by the congregation the bullock is a burnt offering, and the sin offering is a kid of the goats.",
    "text": "KJV Leviticus 4:13: “And if the whole congregation of Israel sin through ignorance, and the thing be hid from the eyes of the assembly, and they have done somewhat against any of the commandments of the Lord concerning things which should not be done” KJV 4:14: “then the congregation shall offer a young bullock for the sin” KJV 4:21: “it is a sin offering for the congregation” KJV Numbers 15:22: “And if ye have erred, and not observed all these commandments” KJV Numbers 15:24: “if ought be committed by ignorance without the knowledge of the congregation, that all the congregation shall offer one young bullock for a burnt offering”; “and one kid of the goats for a sin offering” Hebrew (WLC) Leviticus 4:14: וְהִקְרִ֨יבוּ הַקָּהָ֜ל פַּ֤ר בֶּן־בָּקָר֙ לְחַטָּ֔את [and the assembly shall offer a young bull for a sin offering]. Numbers 15:24: וְעָשׂ֣וּ כָל־הָעֵדָ֡ה פַּ֣ר בֶּן־בָּקָר֩ אֶחָ֨ד לְעֹלָ֜ה [and all the congregation shall offer one young bull for a burnt offering]; וּשְׂעִיר־עִזִּ֥ים אֶחָ֖ד לְחַטָּֽת [and one male goat for a sin offering]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) Leviticus 4:14: καὶ προσάξει ἡ συναγωγὴ μόσχον ἐκ βοῶν ἄμωμον περὶ τῆς ἁμαρτίας [and the congregation shall bring an unblemished calf of the herd for the sin]. Numbers 15:24: μόσχον ἕνα ἐκ βοῶν ἄμωμον εἰς ὁλοκαύτωμα [one unblemished calf of the herd for a whole burnt offering]; καὶ χίμαρον ἐξ αἰγῶν ἕνα περὶ ἁμαρτίας [and one kid of the goats for sin]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/3/4/, https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/4/15/, https://ebible.org/grcbrent/LEV04.htm and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/NUM15.htm.",
    "reasoning": "Both laws deal with the congregation as a whole, with an act done in ignorance and hidden from it. Leviticus requires one animal, a bullock, and it is the sin offering. Numbers requires two animals: the bullock is a burnt offering, and a goat is the sin offering. The animal used as the sin offering is different, and so is the number of animals.",
    "scope": "No tag is proposed: the Hebrew and Brenton’s Greek agree with the KJV in both verses. The two can be reconciled if they cover different cases. Leviticus 4:13 speaks of doing “things which should not be done”, and Numbers 15:22 of having “not observed all these commandments”, so one may concern acts and the other omissions; neither passage says that it is limited in that way or refers to the other. No claim is made about which law is older or about practice. Two published records cite these verses for other points and do not compare the two offerings. The Hebrew quoted is the Westminster Leningrad Codex digital text. A digital named edition is not proof that every manuscript agrees; other Hebrew manuscripts were not examined. The Greek is Brenton’s printed edition of the Septuagint, an ancient Greek translation tradition of the Old Testament. It is not a critical apparatus and does not show that all Greek witnesses agree or which reading is original. English in square brackets is the researcher’s plain rendering, not a KJV quotation and not a lexicon entry.",
