    "title": "“Slew of their foes seventy and five thousand” — the Greek has fifteen thousand",
    "status": "Context",
    "summary": "The KJV, with the Hebrew, says the Jews in the king’s provinces slew seventy-five thousand of their foes. Brenton’s Greek of the same verse says fifteen thousand.",
    "text": "KJV Esther 9:16: “and slew of their foes seventy and five thousand, but they laid not their hands on the prey” Hebrew (WLC) 9:16: וְהָרֹג֙ בְּשֹׂ֣נְאֵיהֶ֔ם חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה וְשִׁבְעִ֖ים אָ֑לֶף [and slew of those that hated them five and seventy thousand]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 9:16: ἀπώλεσαν γὰρ αὐτῶν μυρίους πεντακισχιλίους τῇ τρισκαιδεκάτῃ τοῦ Ἀδὰρ, καὶ οὐδὲν διήρπασαν. [for they destroyed fifteen thousand of them on the thirteenth of Adar, and plundered nothing]. The figures for Shushan agree in the three texts: KJV 9:6 “five hundred men”, Greek ἄνδρας πεντακοσίους; KJV 9:15 “three hundred men”, Greek ἄνδρας τριακοσίους. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/17/9/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/ESG09.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The Hebrew and the KJV give one figure for the provinces and the Greek gives another, one fifth of it. The two figures cannot both be the number slain.",
