    "summary": "The KJV, with the Hebrew, says Job offered burnt offerings according to the number of his children. Brenton’s Greek adds a further offering: one calf for sin, for their souls.",
    "text": "KJV Job 1:5: “and offered burnt offerings according to the number of them all: for Job said” Hebrew (WLC) 1:5: וְהֶעֱלָ֣ה עֹלֹות֮ מִסְפַּ֣ר כֻּלָּם֒ כִּ֚י אָמַ֣ר אִיֹּ֔וב [and offered up burnt offerings, the number of them all; for Job said]. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 1:5: καὶ προσέφερε περὶ αὐτῶν θυσίας, κατὰ τὸν ἀριθμὸν αὐτῶν, καὶ μόσχον ἕνα περὶ ἁμαρτίας περὶ τῶν ψυχῶν αὐτῶν· ἔλεγε γὰρ Ἰὼβ [and offered sacrifices for them, according to their number, and one calf for sin for their souls; for Job said]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/18/1/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/JOB01.htm.",
