    "summary": "The KJV asks whether there is any taste in the white of an egg. Brenton’s Greek of the same verse asks whether there is taste in empty words, and has bread where the KJV has “that which is unsavoury”.",
    "text": "KJV Job 6:6: “Can that which is unsavoury be eaten without salt? or is there any taste in the white of an egg?” Hebrew (WLC) 6:6: הֲיֵאָכֵ֣ל תָּ֭פֵל מִבְּלִי־מֶ֑לַח אִם־יֶשׁ־טַ֝֗עַם בְּרִ֣יר חַלָּמֽוּת. Septuagint (Brenton Greek) 6:6: Εἰ βρωθήσεται ἄρτος ἄνευ ἁλός; εἰ δὲ καὶ ἔστι γεῦμα ἐν ῥήμασι κενοῖς; [Shall bread be eaten without salt? and is there indeed taste in empty words?] Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/18/6/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/JOB06.htm.",
