    "summary": "The KJV has “Thou shalt increase my greatness, and comfort me on every side”. Brenton’s Greek has “thou didst multiply thy righteousness”, comfort, and a clause that brings the speaker “again out of the depths of the earth”.",
    "text": "KJV Psalms 71:20: “shalt bring me up again from the depths of the earth” KJV 71:21: “Thou shalt increase my greatness, and comfort me on every side.” Hebrew (WLC) 71:21: תֶּ֤רֶב ׀ גְּֽדֻלָּתִ֗י וְתִסֹּ֥ב תְּֽנַחֲמֵֽנִי. Brenton’s Greek 70:21: Ἐπλεόνασας τὴν δικαιοσύνην σου, καὶ ἐπιστρέψας παρεκάλεσάς με, καὶ ἐκ τῶν ἀβύσσων τῆς γῆς πάλιν ἀνήγαγές με [Thou hast multiplied thy righteousness, and having turned thou didst comfort me, and out of the depths of the earth thou didst bring me up again]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/71/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA070.htm.",
