    "summary": "In the KJV and the Hebrew, they shall fear God while sun and moon last. In Brenton’s Greek, “he” shall continue with the sun and before the moon, to generations of generations.",
    "text": "KJV Psalms 72:5: “They shall fear thee as long as the sun and moon endure, throughout all generations.” Hebrew (WLC) 72:5: יִֽירָא֥וּךָ עִם־שָׁ֑מֶשׁ וְלִפְנֵ֥י יָ֝רֵ֗חַ דֹּ֣ור דֹּורִֽים. Brenton’s Greek 71:5: καὶ συμπαραμενεῖ τῷ ἡλίῳ, καὶ πρὸ τῆς σελήνης γενεὰς γενεῶν [and he shall abide with the sun, and before the moon, generations of generations]. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/72/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA071.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The KJV verb is “fear”, with an object “thee” and a plural subject. The Greek verb is “abide with”, with a singular subject and no “thee”. The time expressions (with the sun, before the moon, generations) are alike.",
