    "text": "KJV Psalms 92:10: “But my horn shalt thou exalt like the horn of an unicorn: I shall be anointed with fresh oil.” Hebrew (WLC) 92:11: בַּ֝לֹּתִ֗י בְּשֶׁ֣מֶן רַעֲנָֽן. Brenton’s Greek 91:11: καὶ τὸ γῆράς μου ἐν ἐλέῳ πίονι. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/PSA091.htm) prints: “and mine old age with rich mercy”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/92/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA091.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The KJV clause has a verb of anointing and the substance “fresh oil”. The Greek clause printed has no verb of anointing; its nouns are “my old age” (τὸ γῆράς μου) and “mercy” (ἐλέῳ), the second with the adjective that Brenton’s English renders “rich”.",
