    "text": "KJV Psalms 118:27: “God is the Lord, which hath shewed us light: bind the sacrifice with cords, even unto the horns of the altar.” Hebrew (WLC) 118:27: אִסְרוּ־חַ֥ג בַּעֲבֹתִ֑ים. Brenton’s Greek 117:27: συστήσασθε ἑορτὴν ἐν τοῖς πυκάζουσιν. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/PSA117.htm) prints: “celebrate the feast with thick branches”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/118/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA117.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The KJV gives a command about “the sacrifice” and “cords”. The Greek command has ἑορτήν as its object, the word Brenton’s English renders “feast”, and the means is the phrase ἐν τοῖς πυκάζουσιν, which Brenton’s English renders “with thick branches”. Both texts end at the horns of the altar, so both set the command in an altar setting; they differ in what is bound or kept and with what.",
