    "text": "KJV Psalms 138:8: “The Lord will perfect that which concerneth me: thy mercy, O Lord, endureth for ever: forsake not the works of thine own hands.” Hebrew (WLC) 138:8: יְהוָה֮ יִגְמֹ֪ר בַּ֫עֲדִ֥י. Brenton’s Greek 137:8: Κύριε ἀνταποδώσεις ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/PSA137.htm) prints: “thou shalt recompense them on my behalf”; the Greek words quoted have no pronoun for “them”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/138/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA137.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The KJV verb is “perfect”, with the object “that which concerneth me”. The Greek verb is ἀνταποδώσεις, which Brenton’s English renders “thou shalt recompense”, followed by ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ, “on my behalf”. The KJV states that something will be brought to completion; the Greek states that something will be paid back or requited for the speaker. The rest of the verse (the mercy that endures for ever and the works of his hands) is stated in both texts.",
