    "text": "KJV Psalms 139:15: “My substance was not hid from thee, when I was made in secret, and curiously wrought in the lowest parts of the earth.” Hebrew (WLC) 139:15: לֹא־נִכְחַ֥ד עָצְמִ֗י. Brenton’s Greek 138:15: Οὐκ ἐκρύβη τὸ ὀστοῦν μου ἀπὸ σοῦ … καὶ ἡ ὑπόστασίς μου. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/PSA138.htm) prints: “My bones which thou madest in secret were not hidden from thee, nor my substance”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/19/139/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PSA138.htm.",
    "reasoning": "The KJV has one subject, “my substance”, which is said not to be hid, to have been made in secret and to have been wrought in the lowest parts of the earth. The Greek quoted has a different first subject, τὸ ὀστοῦν μου (“my bone”, which Brenton’s English renders in the plural), which is said not to be hidden and to have been made in secret; “my substance” (ἡ ὑπόστασίς μου) is named as a second item at the end of the verse. So the first noun differs, and the Greek has two named items where the KJV has one.",
