    "summary": "The KJV of Proverbs 28:17 says the man who does violence to a person’s blood shall flee to the pit. Brenton’s Greek says the one who becomes surety for a man charged with murder shall be an exile.",
    "text": "KJV Proverbs 28:17: “A man that doeth violence to the blood of any person shall flee to the pit; let no man stay him.” Hebrew (WLC) 28:17: אָ֭דָם עָשֻׁ֣ק בְּדַם־נָ֑פֶשׁ עַד־בֹּ֥ור יָ֝נ֗וּס. Brenton’s Greek 28:17: Ἄνδρα τὸν ἐν αἰτίᾳ φόνου ὁ ἐγγυώμενος, φυγὰς ἔσται. Brenton’s own English (https://ebible.org/eng-Brenton/PRO28.htm) prints: “He that becomes surety for a man charged with murder shall be an exile, and not in safety”. Fetched from https://bolls.life/get-text/WLC/20/28/ and https://ebible.org/grcbrent/PRO28.htm.",
    "reasoning": "In the KJV the one who flees is the man who does violence to a person’s blood. In the Greek the one who becomes an exile is the person who stands surety for a man charged with murder, and the man charged is the object. So the person who suffers the consequence is a different person in each text.",
